    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 28 Clareville Road, a character-filled three-bedroom semi-detached home with an attached garage, ideally positioned on this mature and highly convenient residential road in Harold's Cross. Offering approximately 85 sq m of residential accommodation, excluding the garage, the property has been well maintained over the years but would now benefit from modernisation, presenting an excellent opportunity to create a stylish home tailored to individual requirements.\n\nThe accommodation retains considerable character, with attractive bay windows, well-proportioned rooms, traditional fireplaces and a pair of interconnecting reception rooms. The ground floor comprises an entrance porch and hall, a living room to the front, a separate dining room and a kitchen overlooking and opening to the rear garden. Upstairs are three bedrooms and a bathroom.\n\nOutside, the front garden is bordered by mature hedging, while the paved rear garden provides a private and easily maintained outdoor space. The attached garage offers valuable storage and excellent potential for conversion to increase the living accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe combination of a particularly desirable location, appealing original character and clear scope for improvement makes Number 28 an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a home they can update, extend and personalise over time.\n\nClareville Road is a mature and highly regarded residential address in Harold's Cross, offering an excellent balance of neighbourhood character and city convenience. Harold's Cross village, with its selection of cafés, shops and everyday amenities, is within easy reach, while Terenure, Rathmines, Portobello and Dublin city centre are also readily accessible.\n\nThe surrounding area offers a broad choice of schools, parks, sporting facilities and public transport services. Harold's Cross Park provides an attractive local amenity, while the nearby villages offer a wide variety of restaurants, cafés and independent shops.\n\nWith its settled residential setting and convenient access to the city, 28 Clareville Road represents an appealing opportunity to create a distinctive home in one of south Dublin's most popular and accessible neighbourhoods."
      },
